    "schema_version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Exact products kept out of the consumer catalog because PharmaGuide does not assess them and cannot score them.",
    "purpose": "Sean decided on 2026-11-02 to remove these labels rather than show a coverage warning: sweeteners, excipients, foods and culinary oils, plus sodium-only labels (sodium earns no credit under ruling D22, and BHB and D-aspartate labels print sodium with no amount of the compound). Every one had mapped_coverage 0.0 and no catalog safety finding.",
    "scope": "Fires only for an exact dsld_id in build_final_db.validate_export_contract. Scoring and enrichment are unaffected. A new label of the same product has a new dsld_id and is not excluded until it is added here.",
    "fail_safe_policy": "A listed product whose product_safety_status is anything other than no_known_catalog_concern stays in the catalog, so an exclusion can never hide a safety finding.",
    "last_updated": "2026-11-02",
    "total_entries": 86,
    "loaded_by": "scripts/build_final_db.py via _catalog_exclusions"
  },
